<!--Post: 2351--><!--Time: 1103567830-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2351"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 10:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have started a petition to remove Lt. Landwehr from the BTK taskforce. I know some may disagree with this approach, so don&#39;t sign if you don&#39;t want to. But I also know many, many others that are as frustrated as I am with his handling, &#40;or mishandling&#41;, of the case.  <BR> <BR>Please, at least take the time to read the petition and post on the discussion board if you wish. Here is the link: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ipetitions.com/campaigns/remove_landwehr/" target=_top>http://www.ipetitions.com/campaigns/remove_landweh r/</a> <BR>  <BR>   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2351-->
<!--Post: 2706--><!--Time: 1103965550-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2706"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 1:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How has the case been mishandled? I don&#39;t see any evidence of that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2706-->
<!--Post: 2977--><!--Time: 1104351239-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2977"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 12:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please give me a break on this one. More to the point, give Lt. Landwehr a break and let him do his job, which he knows far more about than anyone who inhabits and posts on this board. He is a trained and experienced professional investgator and the amateur Sherlocks on the boards &#40;all of them, not just this one&#41; need to respect that and back off, unless they are certain they could do better.  <BR>Lt. Landwehr is one of the country&#39;s leading authorities on serial and deviant murder, and he is widely respected across the country and internationally.  <BR>If you want to petition for something, petition to have the police officers in the 1970&#39;s reinvestigated for thier possible involvement, either in the crimes or more likely in establishing a coverup. The entire early investigation reeks of a coverup of some kind - either covering up that BTK was a cop or civilian police employee, or perhaps the family member or close friend of someone in a position of control in the EARLY investigation. Or it reeks of profoundly gross incompetence. Either way it is not Lt. Landwehr&#39;s fault.  <BR>Petitioning to have Lt. Landwehr removed from the case is simply asking that the person called in to clean up after the Tsunami has hit be removed because he hasn&#39;t found Aunt Martha&#39;s engagement ring in the debris. For all the mess he had to clean up, he has done as good a job as anyone could have done, and far better than most would have done. The mound of incompetence and indifference he had to dig through to make any headway was phenominal.  <BR>If you want to blame anyone, blame the police who completely botched the inital investigation, or with even more originial thinking, you might blame BTK for the murders and instead petition that the WPD be given the freedom and resources they need, including search warrants for DNA from ALL of the former members of WPD, both sworn personnel and civillians, and the money to pay for an actual investigation.  <BR>Lt. Landwehr is not the problem. The many years of disastrous investigating he inherited when he took command of the investigation is, at least in part. The constant meddling of rank amateurs and the consequent pressure that creates is as well. For a change lets try to get the WPD and Lt. Landwehr all the support they need and then let them do their jobs without a bunch of amateur interference. Public participation and tips are vitally important - constant public monday morning quartebacking, particularly regarding something the vast majority of the public knows nothing about is destructive to the investigating of the case, and the bringing of justice for the Oteros, and Foxs, and Brights, and Vians, and Wegerles and the victims and families that BTK has continued to kill that we don&#39;t even know about yet. WPD will catch BTK if we help them rather than trying to pull the rug out from under them with ridiculous petitions to influence something we should have absolutley no influence over since we have no expertise what so ever in it. It is professional law enforcement and investigation time. The amateurs need to butt out and help as WPD asks, not as we demand.  <BR>Trust me, Lt. Landwehr wants to catch BTK far more badly than anyone except perhaps the vitctims&#39; families. They are trusting him to bring them justice. We should do the same.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2977-->
<!--Post: 3000--><!--Time: 1104366298-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3000"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 4:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BRAVO, Dpinva! Well said, and I concur.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3000-->
<!--Post: 3001--><!--Time: 1104366903-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3001"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 4:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cops have thankless job to begin with. Let&#39;s all work together on this and not add insult to injury.  Well done Dpinva.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3001-->
<!--Post: 3004--><!--Time: 1104367795-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3004"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Shyra<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Shyra<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 4:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree Dpinva!  Well spoken!  Very good!  That&#39;s great to hear!  Very encouraging!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3004-->
<!--Post: 3019--><!--Time: 1104373665-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3019"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Alobster7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Alobster7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Micaela,  <BR> <BR>I truly understand your frustration about these murders and the investigation.  It sure seems like there should be more progress than there is - especially after 30 yrs.  <BR> <BR>Since I am very new to finding out about this whole situation I am not knowledgeable enough now to sign anything.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3019-->
<!--Post: 3055--><!--Time: 1104391309-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3055"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ozdude<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ozdude<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 11:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I, too, agree, Dpinva. For what it&#39;s worth the petition is meaningless anyway. It is not how the system works. The petition is not worth the paper it&#39;s printed on, or in this case the website. Landwehr is the Lt. over the Homicide unit, which includes btk. He is going nowhere until he chooses to retire. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3055-->
<!--Post: 3085--><!--Time: 1104441162-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3085"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Alobster7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Alobster7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Micaela,  <BR> <BR>Tom asks a very logical question, &#34;How has the case been mishandled?&#34;  Maybe you could provide some insight into this.  True, the case hasn&#39;t been solved for too long a period of time, but to abruptly remove a Lt. I believe you would need some solid evidence of wrongdoing, corruption or whatever.   <BR> <BR>In addition, you might first opt to petition for the man to voluntarily resign.  Then, he is given a chance to leave of his own choosing.   <BR> <BR>I believe your goal is like the rest of us.  Get this idiot, nefarious creep out of his life of freedom, finally solve this case and bring justice to the families.  Hopefully, everyone on this board is unified on this one.   <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3085-->
<!--Post: 3087--><!--Time: 1104443011-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3087"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My first thoughts on reading all of this... <BR> <BR>I grew up in Seattle, always aware of the Green River Killer. He was our local spook story. Now it took HOW MANY YEARS to find him? While yes, there were many mistakes, and I don&#39;t agree with the sentence, at least the police never gave up.The task force was stripped down to just two detectives as the case wore on, and I&#39;m sure similar occurances happened prior to BTK resurfacing. <BR>Unless you know of specific instances of misconduct, and can prove them...I suggest you support the detectives until there is a situation that would outrage any citizen. <BR>Yes, the Seattle tacoma area of washington was frustrated after having 50&#43; women murdered with no progress or effort being shown during the last decade of the investigation, but quietly, the detectives kept going. Were there mistakes? Of course. Were there idiot cops? Of course, but lets not start throwing stones until we know all the facts. <BR>I highly doubt the detectives are just sitting on their butts with a beer, watching sports all day. <BR> <BR>50&#43; women disappeared forever. BTK has taken the lives of many....give the investigators the support they need instead of a cheap shot to their backs. <BR>Why don&#39;t you become a police officer, work your way up to detective status, and then come back and tell me that everythings been bungled in this case.Let&#39;s see you do better. Until then, prove it with documentation that he&#39;s mishandled this, or leave the man alone. <BR>I too don&#39;t know all the details, but in an investigation as vague and complicated as this is, I tend to think most of what can be done, is being done. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3087-->
<!--Post: 3096--><!--Time: 1104449248-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3096"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 3:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I feel the same way, Weeza.  Despite all the profiling there is, no one but BTK will know how accurate that profiling is until &#42;after&#42; his identity is revealed. <BR> <BR>There may not be enough funding for the police and they only have so much evidence to work with.  All the theorizing done on this site is probably just the tip of the iceburg compared to the theorizing and investigating that they&#39;ve done over the years.  It would drive me nuts.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3096-->
<!--Post: 3363--><!--Time: 1104825555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3363"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 11:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I do not know if Officer Landwher should be removed from the case or not.  But even if I thought he should I would not sign the petition as I am not a citizen of Wichita.  It is not up to me, here in Oklahoma, to decide for the Wichitans if they are or are not satisfied with the actions of their police.  I do not believe any non-citizen of Wichita has any business signing the petition.  Now any citizens of the city who wish to circulate such a petition and present it to city officials should do so.  I&#39;ve got enough political criticising to do in my own state of Oklahoma, we just elected the craziest extremist in the US Senate to represent us.  Petition,  ,  ,  ,hmmmmmmmmmm?????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3363-->
<!--Post: 3721--><!--Time: 1105159985-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3721"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 8:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike,  <BR> <BR>He is not <i>Officer </i>Lanwehr, he is <i>Lt.</i> Landwehr. He worked his butt off for his rank and position, and has the expertise and experience to go with it. Please use his PROPER rank and title - it is common courtesy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3721-->
<!--Post: 3727--><!--Time: 1105160960-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3727"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Gotcha<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Gotcha<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 9:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->take a pill dpinva, I think Landwehr could speak for himself if he so choses!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
